---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';

const updated = 'September 2026';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Privacy"
  kicker="How we handle your information"
  lead="What VMSNA collects, who can see it, and how to have it removed."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container container-narrow prose">
      <p class="updated">Last updated {updated}</p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>
        When you apply for membership we collect your name, contact details,
        address, native place, profession, and the same for your spouse and
        children if you choose to provide them. When you submit a support
        request or contact form, we collect what you write in it.
      </p>

      <h2>Who can see it</h2>
      <p>
        Your membership application is visible to the committee members who
        review it. In the member directory you choose between:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Full profile</strong> — other approved members can see your
          name, city and state, native place, profession and contact details.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Limited profile</strong> — other members see only your name
          and state.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Your street address, postcode and any details about your children are
        never shown in the directory, at either setting. The directory is
        available only to approved members who are signed in; it is not public
        and it is not indexed by search engines.
      </p>

      <h2>Support requests</h2>
      <p>
        Education, medical, employment and other assistance requests are read
        only by the committee members who handle them. They are not visible to
        other members and are not published. You do not need an account to
        submit one.
      </p>

      <h2>Payments</h2>
      <p>
        Membership and donation payments are processed by Stripe. Card details
        are entered on Stripe's own systems and never reach vmsna.org. We store
        a record of what was paid and when, not your card number.
      </p>

      <h2>Email</h2>
      <p>
        We email you about your application, your membership, and the events and
        announcements you have opted into. We do not sell or share your details
        with anyone outside VMSNA.
      </p>

      <h2>Changing or deleting your information</h2>
      <p>
        You can edit your profile and change your directory privacy setting at
        any time from your account. You can delete your account yourself, which
        removes your membership record and your directory entry. Some records —
        payment history, for example — are retained where we are required to
        keep them.
      </p>
      <p>
        To ask a question about your data, or to have something removed, write
        to <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        Where members list children as part of a family membership, those
        details are visible only to the reviewing committee and are never shown
        in the directory. Photographs that identify children are kept behind
        member sign-in rather than published publicly.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</PageLayout>

<style>
  .updated {
    font-size: var(--t-sm);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin-bottom: var(--s-6);
  }

  .prose h2 {
    font-size: var(--t-xl);
    margin-block: var(--s-6) var(--s-3);
  }

  .prose h2:first-of-type {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .prose p + p,
  .prose ul + p {
    margin-top: var(--s-4);
  }

  .prose ul {
    margin: var(--s-3) 0 0;
    padding-left: var(--s-5);
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--s-2);
  }
</style>
